      "pins": ["U2.1"],
      "nets": ["I2C2_SCL_FCC", "I2C2_SDA_FCC", "+3.3V"],
      "observed": "On the FCC Peripherals sheet the PWM driver U2 (PCA9685PW) carries the note 'I2C address: 0x41', and its address-strapping pin A0 (pin 1) is tied to +3.3V while A1-A5 are tied to GND, producing a 7-bit address of 0x41.",
      "expected": "The design specification's component table states the PWM driver is 'NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40', i.e. A0 should be strapped low (to GND) so the device responds at 0x40.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "PWM/servo driver | FCCPeripherals | NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U2 PCA9685PW ... 'I2C address: 0x41' with A0 (pin 1) connected to +3.3V and A1-A5 to GND (FCC Peripherals sheet)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The PWM/servo driver sits at 0x41 instead of the intended 0x40. Firmware written against the specified address 0x40 will not acknowledge the PCA9685, so the 16-channel servo/PWM output bank fails to initialise and the servos cannot be driven.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build otherwise matches the specification (correct MCUs, sensor set, regulator topology, and the documented barometer RESET/EOC pin swap), but the PCA9685 PWM driver is strapped to I2C address 0x41 (A0 tied high) whereas the spec's component table intends 0x40, a deviation that would prevent the servo driver from being found at the expected address."
}

